{"name":"Aurora","hex":"#ebd147","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Aurora","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Roman goddess of the dawn; equivalent of the Greek Eos. Sister of Luna and Sol.","A female given name from Latin, in regular use since the 19th century."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Aurora"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aurora","blocks":[{"text":"An aurora is a natural light display in Earth's upper atmosphere caused by charged particles from the Sun colliding with atoms in the atmosphere. These collisions excite oxygen and nitrogen, which then emit light of different colours such as green, red, and purple. When observed in high-latitude regions they are called polar lights and aurora polaris. In the Arctic they are called the northern lights or aurora borealis; in the Antarctic, the term southern lights or aurora australis is used. Auroras display dynamic patterns of radiant light that appear as curtains, rays, spirals or dynamic flickers covering the entire sky."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Aurora_borealis_over_Eielson_Air_Force_Base%2C_Alaska.jpg/330px-Aurora_borealis_over_Eielson_Air_Force_Base%2C_Alaska.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aurora","wikidata":"Q40609"},{"title":"Aurora (singer)","blocks":[{"text":"Aurora Aksnes, known mononymously as AURORA, is a Norwegian singer, songwriter and record producer. Known for blending electropop, folk, and art pop, she has been described as a pioneer of the Norwegian art pop scene and dubbed the \"Fairy of Pop\". She started writing songs and learning dance at age six, and gained recognition as a teenager after a classmate posted her music online without her knowledge. Initially trained on the piano, she later learned percussion and production."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/AURORA%2C_Ravnedalen_Live_festival%2C_Kristiansand%2C_Norway_%2853867200364%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-AURORA%2C_Ravnedalen_Live_festival%2C_Kristiansand%2C_Norway_%2853867200364%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aurora_(singer)","wikidata":"Q19329827"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Flames_in_the_sky.jpg/500px-Flames_in_the_sky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Flames_in_the_sky.jpg/1280px-Flames_in_the_sky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Flames_in_the_sky.jpg/500px-Flames_in_the_sky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlames_in_the_sky.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/G5_aurora_over_Tuntorp%2C_Lysekil_Municipality_15.jpg/500px-G5_aurora_over_Tuntorp%2C_Lysekil_Municipality_15.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/G5_aurora_over_Tuntorp%2C_Lysekil_Municipality_15.jpg/1280px-G5_aurora_over_Tuntorp%2C_Lysekil_Municipality_15.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/G5_aurora_over_Tuntorp%2C_Lysekil_Municipality_15.jpg/500px-G5_aurora_over_Tuntorp%2C_Lysekil_Municipality_15.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AG5_aurora_over_Tuntorp%2C_Lysekil_Municipality_15.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Aurora_australis_ISS.jpg/500px-Aurora_australis_ISS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Aurora_australis_ISS.jpg/500px-Aurora_australis_ISS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAurora_australis_ISS.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Antarctic_aurora_ESA313457.jpg/500px-Antarctic_aurora_ESA313457.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Antarctic_aurora_ESA313457.jpg/1280px-Antarctic_aurora_ESA313457.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Antarctic_aurora_ESA313457.jpg/500px-Antarctic_aurora_ESA313457.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Earth's night-side upper atmosphere appears from the bottom as bands of afterglow illuminating the troposphere in orange with silhouettes of clouds at the top, and the stratosphere in white and blue at the top of the middle. Next, the mesosphere (pink area) extends to the orange and faintly green line of the lowest airglow, at about one hundred kilometres at the edge of space and the lower edge of the thermosphere (invisible). Continuing with green and red bands of auroras stretching over several hundred kilometres.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAntarctic_aurora_ESA313457.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Aurora_shapes.jpg/500px-Aurora_shapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Aurora_shapes.jpg/1280px-Aurora_shapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Aurora_shapes.jpg/500px-Aurora_shapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipe